<title>USA: Xecom sells contracts.</title>
<headline>Xecom sells contracts.</headline>
<dateline>RANCHO MIRAGE, Calif. 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xecom Corp Thursday said it had sold 10 college communication contracts in exchange for the assumption of about $1.0 million of debt related to the contracts.</p>
<p>In a statement Xecom, an operator of telecommunications services principally to U.S. Army and Air Force installations, said the contracts generated about revenues of about $500,000 per year but lost $170,000 for the company on an operating basis.</p>
<p>The identity of the buyer was not disclosed.</p>
